required fields. Reuse ParserUtil validation and map location to the\nexisting Address field. Match whole slash-leading option names while\npreserving edit prefixes and optional tags.\n\nUpdate the usage message and guides, and cover parsing, command\nexecution and storage round trips with regression tests.\n\nRefs #37\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":38,"deletions":26},"docs":{"insertions":16,"deletions":8},"test-code":{"insertions":145,"deletions":155}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-13T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"f8179126bce3987d008e6c0db011b2e6374087c2","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #52 from scoot1234/branch-show-user","messageBody":"Branch show user","tags":["v1.3"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-10-18T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"f33a7fe4ae6ab36b67dcb2b057cd75809db7e3ea","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #59 from scoot1234/branch-add-photos","messageBody":"Branch add photos","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-10-20T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"04270ca6061cd5a4f0fee8f7b0d70d3d667b85bf","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Persist favourite contact selections","messageBody":"Keep favourite identifiers with the address book instead of copying or\nreconstructing profile objects. Preserve selections through JSON saves\nand legacy loads, and remove them when their contact is deleted.\n\nCover copying, duplicate-name suffix reuse, edits and photo round trips.\n\nRefs #62\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":61,"deletions":3},"test-code":{"insertions":129,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"37192b3dd57f77b8775c0d076af59564e18530ae","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Persist bounded recently viewed contact history","messageBody":"Store at most ten distinct contact identifiers in most-recent-first\norder alongside the address book, without duplicating profile records.\nMove repeat visits forward and remove history on deletion or clear.\n\nTest capacity boundaries, copying, edits, duplicate suffix reuse, legacy\nloads and photo-preserving JSON round trips.\n\nRefs #63\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":62,"deletions":3},"test-code":{"insertions":143,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"4392d46104d30db95b55f78d19e848e51c6b4d27","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add favourite contact commands and filtering","messageBody":"Let users mark contacts by name and suffix even outside the current\nfilter, then retrieve their favourites in the selected sort order.\nRefresh an active favourite view immediately when a contact is unmarked.\n\nExercise parsing boundaries, missing targets, repeated operations and\nrestart, delete, suffix-reuse and clear-confirmation workflows.\n\nRefs #62\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":147,"deletions":0},"test-code":{"insertions":230,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"36687bca635ecfbd342f532a7276007d6e70f50a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"List recent contacts after successful profile views","messageBody":"Record show selections at the Logic boundary before saving the address\nbook. Restore the previous history on save errors so an unopened profile\ndoes not become a successful visit.\n\nAdd a recent view ordered by history without replacing the saved sort\npreference. Cover filtering, repeat visits, restart, clear and IO errors.\n\nRefs #63\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":86,"deletions":2},"test-code":{"insertions":242,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"0189e51e0b87d7bd463e7547bcc582b6c75736b1","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Document favourite contact workflows and design","messageBody":"Explain CLI selection, duplicate-name handling, persistence and active\nview behaviour in the user guide and in-app help. Add the implementation\nrationale, a sequence diagram and repeatable manual acceptance checks.\n\nAcknowledge Codex assistance in the developer guide as required by the\ncourse policy.\n\nRefs #62\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":8,"deletions":0},"docs":{"insertions":128,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"d9b950e32f7bbaed86a535c03ed99f1a2904e733","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Document recent contact history and recovery","messageBody":"Describe the ten-contact history contract, successful show selections,\nfilter and sort behaviour, restart persistence and failed-save recovery.\nAdd in-app help, a sequence diagram and manual acceptance scenarios.\n\nAcknowledge Codex assistance and keep the existing profile implementation\nand separately owned last-edited feature outside this scope.\n\nRefs #63\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":5,"deletions":0},"docs":{"insertions":131,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"cbb0545e71a64110057c4fddc3936de30def5b31","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Simplify favourites documentation","messageBody":"Use shorter explanations and clearer examples without changing the\ncommand behaviour or documented edge cases.\n\nRefs #62\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":24,"deletions":27}}},{"hash":"ae94fdffe1d524a3aebe83fbe82d241b6aa6a477","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Simplify recent contacts documentation","messageBody":"Explain history ordering, persistence and save errors in plain language\nwhile keeping the existing behaviour and testing guidance intact.\n\nRefs #63\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":28,"deletions":29}}},{"hash":"0cb53c6e211554c8f139abb9ff4c5c26c7619027","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Clarify development acknowledgement","messageBody":"Use a brief assistance statement while keeping the scope of the\nacknowledgement accurate.\n\nRefs #62\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":1,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"b761046a138ce7148b56b697c4b5d9f80151f351","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Clarify development acknowledgement","messageBody":"Use a brief assistance statement while keeping the scope of the\nacknowledgement accurate.\n\nRefs #63\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":1,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"ffcbf96f6c1446e2d12326bee28dbb7e8634bae2","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Distinguish favourite status and list commands","messageBody":"Rename the commands and their parser to make setting a status distinct\nfrom listing favourites. Keep the public command words unchanged.\n\nUpdate tests and developer diagrams, and document the parser boolean.\n\nRefs #62\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":38,"deletions":33},"other":{"insertions":30,"deletions":29},"docs":{"insertions":24,"deletions":24}}},{"hash":"6ee4b82fe83d9691363bbb119018ee438ac576e9","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Clarify recent-contact ordering and help","messageBody":"Explain why history positions determine the recent view order.\nReplace ambiguous reopening wording with the show command behaviour,\nthe ten-contact limit and persistence across application restarts.\n\nRefs #63\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":4,"deletions":2}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-21T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"9b1cece33f5d6fc63d3adb67de793f0c84d68fc1","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Report changed and unchanged favourite status clearly","messageBody":"Use action-based feedback when a contact is added to or removed from\nfavourites, and explicit unchanged-state messages for repeated commands.\nKeep both operations idempotent and preserve active-view refreshes.\n\nCover all four status outcomes and suffixed names in regression tests.\nUpdate the user guide, developer guide and sequence diagram.\n\nRefs #62\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":15,"deletions":5},"docs":{"insertions":12,"deletions":3},"test-code":{"insertions":16,"deletions":5}}},{"hash":"24d2e6b89b5263b3014d8c7a43d59f8e548e525d","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge upstream master into recent contacts","messageBo